# Git Commit Message Format

## Structure

```
<type>(<scope>): <subject>

<body>

<footer>
```

## Type (lowercase only)

`feat` `fix` `refactor` `docs` `test` `ci` `change` `remove` `revert` `release` `dev` `customer`

## Scope

Lowercase component or directory name: `audio_stream`, `esp_service`, `examples`, `docs`, etc.
Do NOT prefix with `component/`.

## Subject rules

- Start with imperative verb: `Add` / `Fix` / `Remove` / `Change` / `Improve` / `Update`
- Capitalize first letter, no period at end
- Max 50 characters
- Present tense: "Fix bug" not "Fixed bug"

## Body (optional)

- Use when subject alone is insufficient
- No indentation; blank line separates from subject
- Last sentence has no trailing period
- No internal ticket references (e.g. no `AUD-1234`)

## Footer (optional)

Close public GitHub issues with full URL:
```
Closes https://github.com/espressif/esp-adf/issues/XXXX
```

## Examples

```
feat(audio_board): Add esp32_s3_korvo2_v3 board configurations
```

```
fix(audio_pipeline): Fix startup timeout issue

The read/write sync semaphore was released too early, allowing a
higher-priority task to write data before the flag was updated
```

```
refactor(esp_service): Restructure source layout and add Kconfig controls
```
